---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---

<Layout title="About | Jevon Lipsey" description="About Jevon Lipsey, Ph.D. student at Colorado School of Mines MIRRORLab.">
  <div class="space-y-10 max-w-4xl">
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 font-mono">Background, research context, and curriculum vitae.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[1fr_minmax(220px,280px)] gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="reading-body order-2 md:order-1 space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200">
        <p>
          I am a Computer Science Ph.D. student at the <strong>Colorado School of Mines</strong> in the <strong>MIRROЯLab</strong>, advised by <strong>Dr. Tom Williams</strong>. My research focuses on <strong>Human-Robot Interaction (HRI)</strong> in shared civic spaces like public libraries and classrooms. I study how physical embodiment shapes perceived judgment and engagement during sensitive conversations—testing where interactive agents can meaningfully expand access, and where human relationships should never be replaced.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prior to Mines, I earned my B.A. in Computer Science from <strong>Colorado College</strong> (GPA 3.92, Steven Janke, Euclid Scholar awards recognizing academic rigor in CS). My undergraduate research spanned algorithmic fairness and computational redistricting, neurosymbolic reasoning (published at AAAI-25 and PMLR 2025), and cultural humanities work on Midwestern Hip Hop with Oxford University Press.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside academic research, I work in creative computing and full-stack engineering. My work includes building <strong>Featherweight</strong>, an automated eBird observation ranker (Vue.js/FastAPI), developing <strong>Pocket8</strong>, an open-source iOS PICO-8 engine wrapper, and experimenting with real-time web shaders and 3D graphics.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 text-sm">
          Outside the lab, I spend time tinkering with my homelab server, handheld emulation, videography, and other creative coding projects. Away from the desk, I love city biking and exploring the city.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="group relative w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-muted/20 order-1 md:order-2 isolate">
        <img src="/professional-pic.webp" alt="Jevon Lipsey" class="w-full h-auto object-cover grayscale contrast-125 transition-transform duration-700 ease-out group-hover:grayscale-0 group-hover:scale-105 will-change-transform" />
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none ring-1 ring-inset ring-black/5 dark:ring-white/10 rounded-xl z-10"></div>
        <figcaption class="absolute bottom-3 right-3 z-20 px-2.5 py-1 bg-background/90 dark:bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-md border border-border rounded text-[10px] font-mono text-foreground uppercase tracking-widest opacity-0 translate-y-2 group-hover:opacity-100 group-hover:translate-y-0 transition-all duration-500 ease-out">
          Jevon Lipsey
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-border pt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-xs font-mono">
      <a href={SITE.links.cv} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="ink-bleed-link">curriculum vitae (pdf) ↗</a>
      <a href={SITE.links.resume} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="ink-bleed-link">resume (pdf) ↗</a>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.academic}`} class="ink-bleed-link">academic &middot; {SITE.emails.academic} ↗</a>
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.personal}`} class="ink-bleed-link">personal &middot; {SITE.emails.personal} ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
